{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-12549" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given $P(A)=0.25$, $P(B)=0.75$, $P(A\\cup B)=0.8$, determine whether  $A$ and $B$ are mutually exclusive events." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041669/state.json" "file_sha256" "5d293e9ea1e1e93ba2387c003d22b146f94c69ee205546af210f9fe99cd41cb9"} {"question" "q-12549" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To check if $A$ and $B$ are mutually exclusive, we must check that $P(A\\cap B)=0.$\n\nWe can calculate $P(A\\cap B)$ using the addition law:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(A\\cup B) & =P(A)+P(B)-P(A\\cap B) \\\\ 0.8 & =0.25+0.75-P(A\\cap B) \\\\ P(A\\cap B) & =0.25+0.75-0.8 \\\\  & =0.2\\ne 0.\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $A$ and $B$ are not mutually exclusive events." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041669/state.json" "file_sha256" "5d293e9ea1e1e93ba2387c003d22b146f94c69ee205546af210f9fe99cd41cb9"} {"question" "q-12549" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041669/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "d20eeb8b56b42bb3f2cd469a7a29d4ee756cf637f8c6d9aa05b7717029d02da5"} {"question" "q-12549" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041669/state.json" "file_sha256" "5d293e9ea1e1e93ba2387c003d22b146f94c69ee205546af210f9fe99cd41cb9"} {"question" "q-12549" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "$A$ and $B$ are mutually exclusive events, since $P(A\\cap B)=0$"] ["text" "$A$ and $B$ are not mutually exclusive events, since $P(A)\\cdot P(B)<P(A\\cup B)$"] ["text"